  "name": null,
  "problem": "A travel agency offers three itineraries, itinerary $1,$ itinerary $2,$ and itinerary $3.$ For each itinerary, customers can decide to travel using their own car or the agency's bus.\n\n- Itinerary $1$ is chosen by $60%$ of the customers, and $10%$ of those customers travel by bus.\n\n- Itinerary $2$ is chosen by $20%$ of the customers, and $25%$ of those customers travel by bus.\n\n- Itinerary $3$ is chosen by $20%$ of the customers.\n\nIf $30%$ of all customers travel with children, $50%$ of customers with children choose the bus, and $83%$ of customers that choose the bus travel with children, what is the probability that a randomly chosen customer that chooses itinerary $3$ takes the bus? Round your answer to $3$ decimal places.",
  "worked_solution": "",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
